      "leadSummary": "Bioenergetics unites thermodynamics with chemical reactions that support living work. Energy accounting starts by naming the system and its boundaries. At constant temperature and pressure, Gibbs free-energy changes indicate the direction favored by a specified reaction under the modeled conditions. They do not establi"
